<<hubreturn>>
<<else>>\
Raju bhaiya is radiant. His repaired phone sits on the counter like a trophy   screen a single unbroken pane.

<div class="dialogue">"ARJUN BABA! Anwar bhai ne ₹700 mein kar diya. Tera naam liya toh discount. Camera chal raha hai, WhatsApp mein sab contacts wapas."<span class="gloss-en">Anwar bhai did it for ₹700. I mentioned your name, got a discount.</span></div>

He pushes the cutting-chai glass back and replaces it with a full one. "Aaj se tera hafte bhar ka offer. Full chai."<span class="gloss-en">Your week-long offer starts today. Full tea.</span>

He leans in. <div class="dialogue">"Kal udaas tha. Aaj   aaj kuch ho gaya. Jab cheeni zyada maangta hai toh dukhi hota hai. Aaj cheeni nahi maangi. Matlab dil mein meetha hai already."<span class="gloss-en">Yesterday you were sad. Today something's happened. When you ask for extra sugar, you're unhappy. Today you didn't. Which means there's already sweetness in your heart.</span></div>

A poet disguised as a tea vendor. You don't argue.

