:: kulkarni_uncle_d2
<<img "katraj_general_store.png" "Kulkarni General Store">>
Kulkarni uncle runs his shop the way some people run intelligence agencies   meticulous records, total surveillance of a three-block radius, a filing system that lives entirely in his head.

<div class="dialogue">"Arjun beta! Woh type-C charger kaisa chal raha hai?"<span class="gloss-en">How's that type-C charger working?</span></div>

"Chal raha hai, uncle. Ek baat poochun   Pataleshwar temple, wahan subah 5 baje log aate hain?"<span class="gloss-en">Working fine. Can I ask   Pataleshwar temple, do people go there at 5 AM?</span>

He peers over his glasses. <div class="dialogue">"Subah 5 baje? Kuch senior citizens jo yoga karte hain. 5 baje courtyard khula hota hai   guard nahi hota, open area hai. Cave 6 baje tak locked. Koi nahi hota 5 baje. Privacy milegi."<span class="gloss-en">A few senior citizens who do yoga. At 5 the courtyard's open   no guard, open area. Cave locked till 6. Nobody's there at 5. You'll get privacy.</span></div>

"UNCLE. It's not "

<div class="dialogue">"Beta, main saath saal se students ko snacks bech raha hoon. 'Temple jaana hai 5 baje' is new. Usually it's 'sinhagad fort sunrise trek.' Same result, better alibi."<span class="gloss-en">Son, I've been selling students snacks for seven years. "Going to the temple at 5" is new.</span></div>

<<run setup.flag("kulkarni_talked")>>
<<run setup.flag("temple_info")>>
